   <h2>Correcting aerosol bias in satellite CO₂ retrievals</h2>
-  <p class="intro">MethaneSAT measures methane at high resolution, and its CO₂ product is currently used only as a proxy for the methane retrieval. My research asks whether we can remove the bias that aerosol scattering introduces into those CO₂ retrievals, so that MethaneSAT could also quantify regional CO₂ fluxes. Each stage below grew out of what the previous one could not solve.</p>
+  <p class="intro">MethaneSAT is a satellite built to measure methane. My research asks whether we can remove the error that aerosols (haze, dust, smoke) introduce into its CO₂ measurements, so it could also track regional CO₂ emissions. Each stage grew out of what the previous one could not solve.</p>
 
