         <div class="meta"><span><b>Context</b> Graduate course project (EPS 200) feeding into my research</span><span><b>Guidance</b> Prof. Steven C. Wofsy, Eleanor Walker</span></div>
-        <p>To understand the physics the regression missed, I took a basic two-stream radiative transfer toy model from my advisor and extended it into a tool for studying how aerosols, surface brightness and gas absorption interact. The goal was to see how errors in assumed aerosol or albedo turn into errors in retrieved surface pressure, and to make the model fast enough to run on millions of satellite pixels.</p>
