         <h3>Using surface variation to correct light-path errors</h3>
         <div class="meta"><span><b>Advisors</b> Prof. Christian Frankenberg, Prof. Steven C. Wofsy</span></div>
-        <p>With a full radiative transfer model (vSmartMOM), I simulated satellite CO₂ retrievals under different aerosols, surfaces and viewing geometries, and developed a correction that works under noise levels similar to MethaneSAT's.</p>
+        <p class="summary">I simulated satellite CO₂ measurements with a full radiative transfer model (vSmartMOM) and built a correction that uses one fact: over a small area the air is roughly uniform, while the ground underneath varies sharply. That contrast lets the method estimate the aerosol effect and remove it.</p>
